{{!
    @template theme_nit/navbar_gear_menu

    The navbar's gear button and the dropdown it opens: the groups the
    administrator wrote into Appearance → Advanced theme settings → "Gear menu"
    (theme_nit/gearmenuitems — see theme_nit\local\gear_menu for the line
    syntax), with core's edit-mode switch relocated in after the first group.
    Rendered by theme_nit\output\core_renderer::navbar_gear_menu(), which
    returns nothing at all when there is no group and no switch — so a guest,
    or a student with nothing to open, has no gear on the bar.

    Every group is a `.nit-navmenu-group`; the stylesheet draws the divider
    above each one but the first child of the panel, so the first group sits
    flush under the top and the ones after it — and the switch between — are
    separated by a line.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * groups - [{heading, hasheading, isfirst, items:[{text, url, isactive}]}], already
               filtered to what this viewer may see; empty groups are not passed
    * hasgroups - bool, whether groups has anything in it
    * editswitch - HTML of core's edit-mode switch, or ''

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasgroups": true,
        "groups": [
            {"heading": "Navigation", "hasheading": true, "isfirst": true, "items": [
                {"text": "My courses", "url": "https://example.com/my/courses.php", "isactive": true}
            ]},
            {"heading": "Management", "hasheading": true, "items": [
                {"text": "Manage coupons", "url": "https://example.com/local/nit_commerce/manage_coupons.php", "isactive": false}
            ]}
        ],
        "editswitch": ""
    }
}}
<div class="dropdown nit-navmenu d-flex align-items-center">
    <a href="#" role="button" id="nit-navmenu-toggle" class="btn nit-navbar-icon" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{#str}}navigation, core{{/str}}">
        <i class="icon fa fa-gear fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}navigation, core{{/str}}</span>
    </a>
    <div class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end nit-navbar-dropdown" aria-labelledby="nit-navmenu-toggle">
        {{#groups}}
            <div class="nit-navmenu-group">
                {{#hasheading}}<h6 class="dropdown-header">{{{heading}}}</h6>{{/hasheading}}
                {{#items}}
                    <a class="dropdown-item{{#isactive}} active{{/isactive}}" href="{{{url}}}" {{#isactive}}aria-current="true"{{/isactive}}>{{{text}}}</a>
                {{/items}}
            </div>
            {{#isfirst}}
                {{! Edit-mode toggle (moved from the bar), after the first group.
                    The wrapper is `:empty` when core returns no switch — CSS
                    then hides it, so no stray row. }}
                <div class="nit-navmenu-editswitch">{{{ editswitch }}}</div>
            {{/isfirst}}
        {{/groups}}
        {{^hasgroups}}
            {{! No group survived the viewer's rules (or the setting is empty):
                the switch is all there is, and the renderer only got this far
                because there is one. }}
            <div class="nit-navmenu-editswitch">{{{ editswitch }}}</div>
        {{/hasgroups}}
    </div>
</div>
